---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../lib/site.ts'
import '../styles/prose.css'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description={`What ${SITE_TITLE} is, who it is for, and how the lessons are put together.`}
>
  <div class="container-page section">
    <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        {SITE_TITLE} is a free, public collection of lessons on programming languages and
        technologies. There is no account, no paywall and no upsell — every page is open to
        anyone.
      </p>

      <h2>Why it exists</h2>
      <p>
        Most language documentation is written as reference material: complete, precisely worded,
        and organised for people who already know what they are looking for. That is the right
        shape for a manual and the wrong shape for learning. Tutorials often swing too far the
        other way, walking through steps without ever explaining why any of it works.
      </p>
      <p>
        These lessons aim at the middle. Each one takes a single idea, explains the model behind
        it, shows the code, and then asks you a question about it.
      </p>

      <h2>How the lessons work</h2>
      <p>
        A lesson is a short read — usually well under ten minutes — built around one concept. Code
        examples are real and runnable rather than illustrative pseudocode. At the end of each
        section there is a question with immediate feedback and an explanation, whichever way you
        answered.
      </p>
      <p>
        The questions are checkpoints, not tests. Nothing is scored, nothing is tracked, and no
        result leaves your browser. Because the checking happens in the page, the answers are
        visible to anyone who opens developer tools — that is a deliberate trade. The goal is
        helping you learn, not preventing you from cheating at something with no stakes.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If a lesson is wrong, unclear, or out of date, that is worth fixing — see the <a
          href="/contact">contact page</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-title {
    font-size: var(--text-4xl);
    font-weight: 680;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
</style>
